    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2829" root="بظر" body-key="b">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَظَرٌ</span></b>  The <i>having a</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَظْر</span>: (T, S:) or the <i>having
a long</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَظْر</span>: (K:) a subst., (K,) or an inf. n.,
(T,) having no verb, (T, M, *) because it denotes
an inherent quality, not one that is accidental.
(T.) [But see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَظِرَتْ</span>.]

